  "deviations": [
    {
      "item": "engineer defaults for unstated values",
      "detail": "The article does not print the learning rates, batch sizes, epoch counts, the drug-cost weight, the coverage level alpha, the admitted fraction, the trust radius, the number of sparse atoms or the cloning passes. Every such value is a documented engineering default in configs/round/primary.yaml, marked with a comment where it appears."
    },
    {
      "item": "critic-based realisation of the maximisation term",
      "detail": "Eq. (4) maximises the verifier's expectation over the policy. With a flow the expectation has no closed form, so the release maximises a return critic fitted on admitted episodes and keeps the flow-matching term as the density anchor. The deviation is the estimator, not the constraint."
    },
    {
      "item": "constraint normalisation in the dual",
      "detail": "The three costs and the trust region are divided by their budgets before the dual step, so one learning rate serves all four multipliers. This is a reparametrisation of the same Lagrangian."
    },
    {
      "item": "axis anchoring on the theatre",
      "detail": "The three axes are anchored weakly to the generating factors, which only the theatre can supply. On record-level replay there is no anchor and the interventional term carries the axes alone."
    },
    {
      "item": "record-level corpora are not shipped",
      "detail": "VitalDB, MIMIC-IV and eICU-CRD are credentialed. The release ships the theatre, the readers for the official export layouts, and no substituted cohort."
    }
  ]
}
